#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100613 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "288e49b0-f706-54de-86b7-a17248fe2408" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Parallelogram Spanned by Two Non-Parallel Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "fe75d710-2f18-5ddb-9f93-3127d8cec7ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-4437" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\textbf{u}=\\langle 1,2 \\rangle$ and $\\textbf{v}=\\langle 3, -3 \\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(M) &= \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot (-3) - 3 \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&=-9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $\\det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA = \\mid {-9} \\mid = 9\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100614 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0272b8d6-8400-5a6d-b51d-fc6ca84bd166" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Parallelogram Spanned by Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "c824ba23-c39c-5205-81a3-98d2e4b823f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4438" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\textbf{u}=\\langle 3,-2 \\rangle$ and $\\textbf{v}=\\langle 6, -4 \\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(M) &= \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot (-4) - 6 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $\\det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA = \\mid \\,0\\, \\mid = 0\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101435 :knowl